1
00:00:06,740 --> 00:00:08,990
Wonderful. You are wonderful.

2
00:00:08,990 --> 00:00:12,910
Hearin' that from anyone but 
Ram don't make me happy!

3
00:00:23,990 --> 00:00:25,130
Just the best.

4
00:00:26,220 --> 00:00:28,850
I told ya, I don't wanna hear it!

5
00:00:31,890 --> 00:00:36,620
Yo, Big Sis! Yer still standin' 
there like a damn statue?

6
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:37,650
No, I...

7
00:00:38,220 --> 00:00:42,110
Y'know, the boss is countin' on 
you to do your part, too.

8
00:00:42,110 --> 00:00:43,310
So do it!

9
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:51,330
I believe in you!

10
00:00:51,510 --> 00:00:53,460
Damn straight!

11
00:01:18,730 --> 00:01:21,320
Looks like Big Sis took off.

12
00:01:31,460 --> 00:01:32,760
I am the Bowel Hunter...

13
00:01:36,870 --> 00:01:38,790
Elsa Granhiert.

14
00:01:40,370 --> 00:01:43,500
The strongest damn shield in the Sanctuary...

15
00:01:43,980 --> 00:01:46,010
Garfiel Tinzel!

16
00:01:47,620 --> 00:01:51,280
It's my first battle, Boss, and 
I'm makin' a helluva show of it!

17
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:54,270
So you'd damn well better do your part, too!

18
00:02:00,610 --> 00:02:01,840
Why are you here?

19
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:04,610
I'm getting you out of here, Beatrice.

20
00:02:05,390 --> 00:02:10,070
This time, you're gonna let me 
drag you out into the sunlight,

21
00:02:10,350 --> 00:02:14,830
and then we're gonna play until your 
dress is black with mud!

22
00:02:15,270 --> 00:02:17,830
You're taking me out of here?

23
00:02:19,360 --> 00:02:21,280
Mind your own business, I suppose.

24
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:24,240
No one asked you to do such a thing.

25
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:26,930
We don't have time to argue about this.

26
00:02:26,930 --> 00:02:29,960
Do you have any idea 
what's happening outside?

27
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:33,410
I'm aware of the intruder 
in the mansion, I suppose.

28
00:02:33,410 --> 00:02:36,320
But this is a great spirit's 
forbidden library.

29
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:38,240
No matter what threat exists outside—

30
00:02:38,240 --> 00:02:42,220
No, Door Crossing only works on closed doors.

31
00:02:42,220 --> 00:02:43,440
She knows that.

32
00:02:43,440 --> 00:02:46,820
And how does the enemy know 
that weakness, I suppose?

33
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,030
Roswaal told her.

34
00:02:54,160 --> 00:02:55,990
That's how it is.

35
00:02:57,190 --> 00:03:01,800
It means my death was written in 
Roswaal's Tome of Wisdom, I suppose.

36
00:03:05,390 --> 00:03:09,360
Why... Are you... Why is that look on your face?

37
00:03:09,360 --> 00:03:12,250
My fate is already set in stone.

38
00:03:12,250 --> 00:03:16,640
Does that book of yours say you 
have to let that psycho kill you?!

39
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:19,580
It doesn't say anything, I suppose.

40
00:03:20,430 --> 00:03:23,600
My fate is blank, as it has always been.

41
00:03:23,600 --> 00:03:29,030
Then what reason is there for you 
to end up the way Roswaal wants?!

42
00:03:29,030 --> 00:03:33,410
Just decide what to do for yourself, 
like you've always done!

43
00:03:34,030 --> 00:03:36,350
Decide for myself?

44
00:03:38,240 --> 00:03:42,990
What have I ever decided 
for myself before now?

45
00:03:43,730 --> 00:03:47,250
I have continued to obey Mother's 
orders here in this mansion,

46
00:03:47,250 --> 00:03:48,680
all alone.

47
00:03:49,230 --> 00:03:51,820
What part of this did I get to choose?

48
00:03:52,230 --> 00:03:54,770
What has this Beatrice done?

49
00:03:54,770 --> 00:03:55,470
Who is she?

50
00:03:56,620 --> 00:03:58,030
Beatrice...

51
00:03:58,360 --> 00:04:00,870
My life is pure white, I suppose.

52
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:04,220
It's completely blank, well and truly.

53
00:04:04,850 --> 00:04:07,880
This one book was really all I needed.

54
00:04:09,200 --> 00:04:12,440
I do have a soul, after all.

55
00:04:12,930 --> 00:04:15,680
As time passes, I think about many things.

56
00:04:15,680 --> 00:04:18,480
I worry and cease to believe, I suppose.

57
00:04:19,450 --> 00:04:22,610
There were so many nights when 
I couldn't remember Mother's smile,

58
00:04:22,610 --> 00:04:26,750
so I scraped all my memories together 
and tried to cling to them.

59
00:04:27,380 --> 00:04:29,020
There were even times when

60
00:04:29,020 --> 00:04:31,960
I was afraid to be alone and 
wanted to be with someone!

61
00:04:32,670 --> 00:04:35,810
But everyone leaves me behind!

62
00:04:35,810 --> 00:04:39,640
Mother and Roswaal... and Ryuzu, too!

63
00:04:41,210 --> 00:04:45,000
The spirit Beatrice is fated to be alone,

64
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:47,730
to be left behind by everyone else forever.

65
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:50,340
But...

66
00:04:52,160 --> 00:04:55,070
I feel a tiny bit relieved now, I suppose.

67
00:04:56,940 --> 00:05:00,280
If I was mentioned in the Tome of Wisdom,

68
00:05:00,950 --> 00:05:06,460
that means Mother didn't 
forget about me after all.

69
00:05:08,730 --> 00:05:10,370
Give me a break!

70
00:05:11,140 --> 00:05:14,160
You're an idiot! You're just a big idiot!

71
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:16,720
You're so pathetic to watch, it's killing me!

72
00:05:17,270 --> 00:05:19,170
You've had 400 whole years!

73
00:05:19,170 --> 00:05:22,420
Why is something that extreme the 
only answer you could come up with?!

74
00:05:22,420 --> 00:05:27,120
Isn't it possible your mother gave 
you the wrong book by mistake?!

75
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:29,580
You dare insult Mother, I suppose?!

76
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:32,090
She would never make such a stupid mistake!

77
00:05:32,090 --> 00:05:34,110
Can you say that for sure?!

78
00:05:34,330 --> 00:05:39,740
So you really believe that your 
mother gave you a blank book?!

79
00:05:40,200 --> 00:05:43,480
That's... Must you put it that way?

80
00:05:44,030 --> 00:05:47,000
What is it you want me to say, I suppose?

81
00:05:47,220 --> 00:05:49,710
Okay, I'll come right out and say it,

82
00:05:49,710 --> 00:05:52,220
so your dumb mother can hear!

83
00:05:53,460 --> 00:05:58,940
Don't let a blank book and a 400-year-old 
verbal promise rule you forever!

84
00:05:58,940 --> 00:06:02,680
Choose what you want to 
do for yourself, Beatrice!

85
00:06:03,790 --> 00:06:05,370
It's been 400 years!

86
00:06:05,370 --> 00:06:09,890
That's more than enough time for 
you to have one rebellious phase!

87
00:06:09,890 --> 00:06:13,790
No matter what you say, I'm under a contract.

88
00:06:13,790 --> 00:06:16,100
The contract is absolute... which means...

89
00:06:16,100 --> 00:06:18,560
That's rich, coming from 
the one who tried to find

90
00:06:18,560 --> 00:06:21,860
a back door in that contract, then 
wanted to die when it was unbreakable!

91
00:06:22,280 --> 00:06:24,650
If keeping a promise means you die,

92
00:06:24,650 --> 00:06:27,880
I'd rather break that 
promise and keep you alive!

93
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:30,620
Is it so weird that I 
would make that choice?!

94
00:06:31,110 --> 00:06:34,690
Th-That's a very defiant, selfish 
way to think, I suppose.

95
00:06:34,690 --> 00:06:38,910
I know it's defiant, and I know it's selfish!

96
00:06:38,910 --> 00:06:39,340
But...

97
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:43,180
I refuse to compromise on something 
that's important to me!

98
00:06:45,700 --> 00:06:50,180
If... you are... "that person"...

99
00:06:53,810 --> 00:06:56,720
Would you be...

100
00:06:57,560 --> 00:06:59,950
"that person" for me?

101
00:07:01,930 --> 00:07:03,330
Are you dumb?

102
00:07:03,330 --> 00:07:07,450
There's no way I could be whoever 
"that person" is to you.

103
00:07:11,780 --> 00:07:13,550
Unbelievable!

104
00:07:14,050 --> 00:07:15,800
That idiot!

105
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:19,720
Damn that loli and her 
jumping to conclusions!

106
00:07:21,230 --> 00:07:22,380
Natsuki-san?

107
00:07:22,960 --> 00:07:25,920
Why are you... You guys 
should've run away ages ago!

108
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:28,220
Mabeasts! They're already everywhere!

109
00:07:28,610 --> 00:07:31,650
Maylie... But we already accounted for that!

110
00:07:31,650 --> 00:07:34,520
But there's a mabeast that 
this didn't work on at all!

111
00:07:37,490 --> 00:07:39,820
Are you serious? But why...

112
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:49,920
Petra!

113
00:07:51,010 --> 00:07:53,250
Stay exactly as you are!

114
00:07:58,960 --> 00:08:00,270
Wh-What was...

115
00:08:00,270 --> 00:08:02,710
I do apologize, even if it was an emergency.

116
00:08:03,140 --> 00:08:04,930
You aren't hurt, are you?

117
00:08:10,030 --> 00:08:11,920
Nee-sama!

118
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:15,410
Ow!

119
00:08:15,410 --> 00:08:18,430
You saved my life only 
to treat me like that?!

120
00:08:18,430 --> 00:08:21,180
I-I sincerely apologize, Otto-sama.

121
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:24,640
The order of priority suddenly 
became very clear to me.

122
00:08:24,640 --> 00:08:28,560
Women and children, 
the elderly, men, and then Otto?

123
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:32,170
You didn't even put me in the "men" category!

124
00:08:33,780 --> 00:08:37,880
Subaru-sama, I have brought 
her here as requested.

125
00:08:38,990 --> 00:08:40,150
So you did.

126
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:46,460
Thank you for getting her out safe.

127
00:08:47,810 --> 00:08:50,000
Thank you... so much.

128
00:08:51,240 --> 00:08:52,910
I only did what needed to be done.

129
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:55,890
Our more pressing issue now is...

130
00:09:06,730 --> 00:09:09,360
Wow, I'm amazed!

131
00:09:09,360 --> 00:09:13,330
I couldn't believe it when none of 
you died in the midst of all that.

132
00:09:13,560 --> 00:09:14,800
Maylie!

133
00:09:15,140 --> 00:09:18,900
Oh? You don't seem very surprised.

134
00:09:18,900 --> 00:09:20,740
How disappointing.

135
00:09:21,130 --> 00:09:25,240
Still, I'll be taking those maids now.

136
00:09:25,240 --> 00:09:28,300
I'll be especially gentle with Petra-chan.

137
00:09:28,300 --> 00:09:29,850
She's my friend, after all.

138
00:09:30,150 --> 00:09:32,870
Y-Yay! I'm so glad!

139
00:09:32,870 --> 00:09:35,810
If we're really my friend, 
you could even let me go, you know!

140
00:09:35,810 --> 00:09:40,640
We are friends... so you'll play 
with me until the very end, right?

141
00:09:40,640 --> 00:09:41,180
Uh...

142
00:09:41,820 --> 00:09:44,820
Sorry, Subaru! I don't think it worked!

143
00:09:49,850 --> 00:09:54,460
Allow me to handle this girl...
 no, this assassin.

144
00:09:54,930 --> 00:09:56,570
The rest of you can run while I do.

145
00:09:56,570 --> 00:09:58,830
Y-You can't, Frederica-neesama!

146
00:09:59,270 --> 00:10:00,800
I mean, before...

147
00:10:01,350 --> 00:10:02,920
And I finally got to see you again...

148
00:10:05,170 --> 00:10:07,650
No, it will be different this time.

149
00:10:08,100 --> 00:10:11,450
After all, I was prepared to die last time.

150
00:10:12,930 --> 00:10:14,830
But this time, I am not.

151
00:10:15,540 --> 00:10:19,270
I reunited with Garf, my little brother,
 after ten years apart,

152
00:10:19,800 --> 00:10:22,190
and I have such an adorable subordinate now.

153
00:10:22,190 --> 00:10:24,480
There is no greater happiness.

154
00:10:25,120 --> 00:10:27,440
So I will not lose.

155
00:10:30,820 --> 00:10:31,420
Okay.

156
00:10:32,450 --> 00:10:33,740
Frederica!

157
00:10:33,740 --> 00:10:35,610
We'll head to Roswaal's room!

158
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:37,870
Yes, as you wish.

159
00:10:41,120 --> 00:10:44,000
Hey, wait! Don't just decide that yourself!

160
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,200
Petra-chan!

161
00:10:45,200 --> 00:10:46,420
Nyah!

162
00:10:53,030 --> 00:10:54,040
Honored guest...

163
00:10:54,460 --> 00:10:58,810
Please enjoy the finest hospitality 
the Mathers house has to offer.

164
00:10:59,970 --> 00:11:03,200
I won't let you get away with this!

165
00:11:03,200 --> 00:11:04,900
Get them, Rock Piggie!

166
00:11:09,320 --> 00:11:11,940
Please, do come to me.

167
00:11:11,940 --> 00:11:14,700
I am feeling quite harsh at the moment.

168
00:11:15,880 --> 00:11:16,820
Prepare yourself!

169
00:11:21,290 --> 00:11:22,500
What are we gonna do?!

170
00:11:22,780 --> 00:11:25,680
There's an escape route in Roswaal's office!

171
00:11:25,680 --> 00:11:26,800
We'll use that to...

172
00:11:38,850 --> 00:11:39,680
It's here!

173
00:11:39,980 --> 00:11:43,740
Natsuki-san, that's it! The guiltylowe!

174
00:11:43,740 --> 00:11:45,850
The mabeast ward doesn't work on that one!

175
00:11:45,850 --> 00:11:47,700
It's our natural enemy!

176
00:11:53,850 --> 00:11:56,520
It was my teacher and I who started it.

177
00:11:57,020 --> 00:11:59,030
That is the one thing you got wrong,

178
00:11:59,280 --> 00:12:00,400
Emilia-sama.

179
00:12:06,160 --> 00:12:07,410
I've seen the past.

180
00:12:07,990 --> 00:12:09,450
So, up next should be...

181
00:12:15,130 --> 00:12:17,340
<i>Behold an unthinkable present.</i>

182
00:12:27,100 --> 00:12:30,720
Now, Lia, don't shake your 
head around like that.

183
00:12:30,720 --> 00:12:32,350
Just hold still.

184
00:12:32,350 --> 00:12:34,560
Honestly, what am I going to do with you?

185
00:12:37,610 --> 00:12:39,530
Mother Fortuna?

186
00:12:40,530 --> 00:12:43,240
What's wrong? Were you falling asleep?

187
00:12:49,200 --> 00:12:52,200
You're all dressed up today.

188
00:12:52,660 --> 00:12:54,120
You look so pretty!

189
00:12:54,710 --> 00:12:57,210
I wondered what you were about to say.

190
00:12:57,210 --> 00:12:59,380
Don't tease grown-ups like that.

191
00:13:10,220 --> 00:13:12,180
There. You're beautiful now.

192
00:13:12,770 --> 00:13:14,560
Thank you, Mother.

193
00:13:15,810 --> 00:13:17,310
And the mirror...

194
00:13:25,900 --> 00:13:27,110
Emilia?

195
00:13:30,620 --> 00:13:31,700
A visitor!

196
00:13:33,830 --> 00:13:36,580
Good morning, Emilia-sama.

197
00:13:37,330 --> 00:13:39,750
I'm so happy to be greeted by you.

198
00:13:41,130 --> 00:13:42,130
Geuse...

199
00:13:43,760 --> 00:13:45,130
Good morning.

200
00:13:46,340 --> 00:13:47,680
Right on time.

201
00:13:48,300 --> 00:13:50,260
Well, shall we go?

202
00:13:57,190 --> 00:13:57,980
What?

203
00:13:57,980 --> 00:14:01,690
Well... I do hope this doesn't offend you...

204
00:14:01,690 --> 00:14:03,690
How long have we known each other?

205
00:14:03,690 --> 00:14:07,070
Nothing you say to me is going to offend me.

206
00:14:07,990 --> 00:14:09,700
Then, Fortuna-sama...

207
00:14:10,320 --> 00:14:13,120
Your outfit today looks lovely on you.

208
00:14:13,540 --> 00:14:17,330
I found myself a bit captivated by it.

209
00:14:23,550 --> 00:14:25,760
Did I say something rude?

210
00:14:25,760 --> 00:14:27,680
No, not at all.

211
00:14:28,340 --> 00:14:29,760
She's just embarrassed.

212
00:14:30,260 --> 00:14:32,010
Mother is so cute!

213
00:14:32,010 --> 00:14:34,430
Don't just blurt out whatever you want!

214
00:14:34,430 --> 00:14:36,520
How mean-spirited can you be?

215
00:14:36,520 --> 00:14:38,310
Ah, Fortuna-sama.

216
00:14:39,690 --> 00:14:42,520
And Emilia and Geuse-san are with you.

217
00:14:43,020 --> 00:14:44,940
You're such a close-knit family.

218
00:14:44,940 --> 00:14:46,030
We're not—

219
00:14:46,030 --> 00:14:47,900
You are loved by so many.

220
00:14:50,530 --> 00:14:52,660
I... I suppose so.

221
00:15:05,500 --> 00:15:06,550
Isn't it nice?

222
00:15:12,010 --> 00:15:15,760
Oh, come, now. Is your height the 
only part of you that's grown up?

223
00:15:18,270 --> 00:15:20,980
You two are just as close as ever, I see.

224
00:15:21,770 --> 00:15:23,980
Watching you warms my heart.

225
00:15:24,360 --> 00:15:26,030
Why don't you join us?

226
00:15:26,030 --> 00:15:27,780
You could come live with us.

227
00:15:29,240 --> 00:15:30,450
Emilia...

228
00:15:31,320 --> 00:15:32,610
Are you all right?

229
00:15:34,910 --> 00:15:37,790
Your offer makes me very happy, Emilia-sama.

230
00:15:38,500 --> 00:15:41,670
I wish from the bottom of 
my heart that I could do so.

231
00:15:41,670 --> 00:15:44,880
If you could? Why don't you just do it?

232
00:15:44,880 --> 00:15:46,840
Or would I be in the way?

233
00:15:46,840 --> 00:15:48,670
Not at all.

234
00:15:46,840 --> 00:15:48,670
You most certainly would not.

235
00:15:49,470 --> 00:15:51,930
See? You two get along so well!

236
00:15:52,550 --> 00:15:55,890
Fortuna-sama is tasked with 
a very important duty.

237
00:15:56,310 --> 00:15:59,890
If one such as myself were to stay 
with her and it led to rumors,

238
00:15:59,890 --> 00:16:01,480
it would be problematic for her.

239
00:16:02,060 --> 00:16:04,230
I think it's too late for that, though.

240
00:16:05,060 --> 00:16:08,150
Remember what Aunt Tanse and 
the others said earlier?

241
00:16:08,730 --> 00:16:10,490
That we're a close-knit family!

242
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:15,990
I-I thought she was talking 
about the two of you!

243
00:16:15,990 --> 00:16:17,870
You understood, didn't you, Mother?

244
00:16:19,330 --> 00:16:23,290
I think it's a great idea! I really do!

245
00:16:23,790 --> 00:16:26,590
The people of the forest 
won't think it's weird.

246
00:16:26,590 --> 00:16:31,670
I'll never let anyone say it's a bad thing!

247
00:16:33,760 --> 00:16:35,840
I've said what I wanted to say.

248
00:16:36,220 --> 00:16:39,140
I'll leave the rest to you two young folks!

249
00:16:41,390 --> 00:16:45,600
Emilia... Honestly, where 
do you learn these things?

250
00:16:51,490 --> 00:16:53,860
I swear, you are just too cute!

251
00:16:53,860 --> 00:16:57,490
So I see. Emilia-sama has 
grown up healthy and happy.

252
00:16:57,490 --> 00:16:58,950
This truly brings me joy.

253
00:16:58,950 --> 00:17:02,120
Of course she has! She's a 
daughter I can be proud of!

254
00:17:02,120 --> 00:17:04,500
Of course. How could I not see it?

255
00:17:10,880 --> 00:17:14,550
Oh... I think there's something in my eye.

256
00:17:15,220 --> 00:17:16,840
I'm going to go wash it out.

257
00:17:16,840 --> 00:17:18,140
Are you all right?

258
00:17:18,140 --> 00:17:20,970
Be careful you don't lose 
that eye in the process.

259
00:17:20,970 --> 00:17:24,560
You got those lovely purple eyes 
from my brother, after all.

260
00:17:24,560 --> 00:17:27,690
And they're the same pretty color as yours.

261
00:17:31,110 --> 00:17:32,740
Stay that close and wait for me, all right?

262
00:17:33,280 --> 00:17:37,490
P-Please stay super-duper 
close forever and ever.

263
00:17:37,490 --> 00:17:40,490
Yes, of course. You're such a worrywart.

264
00:17:40,490 --> 00:17:43,790
We will wait as long as 
it takes, Emilia-sama.

265
00:17:52,800 --> 00:17:55,380
I love you both.

266
00:18:04,520 --> 00:18:05,810
Emilia?

267
00:18:05,810 --> 00:18:08,190
It's dangerous for you to be up here alone.

268
00:18:08,600 --> 00:18:09,520
Archi...

269
00:18:10,690 --> 00:18:13,530
The bishop is in the forest today, isn't he?

270
00:18:14,110 --> 00:18:15,990
You're not with... oh.

271
00:18:16,740 --> 00:18:18,360
He's over there, I see.

272
00:18:18,360 --> 00:18:20,200
Were you leaving the two of them alone?

273
00:18:20,570 --> 00:18:22,330
Yes, I was.

274
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:26,000
What do you think of the two of them, Archi?

275
00:18:26,410 --> 00:18:28,170
I think they're a nice fit.

276
00:18:28,500 --> 00:18:31,210
Fortuna-sama is very harsh on herself.

277
00:18:31,210 --> 00:18:34,550
I wish she would give more 
thought to her own happiness.

278
00:18:35,090 --> 00:18:38,800
It may be difficult right now, 
but with time, they could...

279
00:18:39,340 --> 00:18:40,090
But...

280
00:18:40,930 --> 00:18:44,060
That world doesn't exist anywhere, does it?

281
00:18:46,020 --> 00:18:47,140
Emilia...

282
00:18:51,520 --> 00:18:53,900
Having beheld an unthinkable present,

283
00:18:54,610 --> 00:18:57,320
did you not wish to live here?

284
00:18:59,360 --> 00:19:02,620
I'm sure you wanted the 
two of them to be happy.

285
00:19:03,120 --> 00:19:05,040
This is your ideal present,

286
00:19:05,410 --> 00:19:07,500
the future you wished for.

287
00:19:07,910 --> 00:19:09,960
Yes, it is.

288
00:19:09,960 --> 00:19:12,250
Fortuna-sama has already passed,

289
00:19:12,250 --> 00:19:14,550
it's unknown whether the bishop lives,

290
00:19:14,550 --> 00:19:16,880
and the people of the forest 
have turned into ice statues.

291
00:19:17,340 --> 00:19:18,050
Yes.

292
00:19:18,050 --> 00:19:20,050
Your homeland is frozen,

293
00:19:20,050 --> 00:19:22,510
you are persecuted by 
people from the outside,

294
00:19:22,510 --> 00:19:26,140
and you had to say goodbye to the 
spirit who was like family to you.

295
00:19:26,140 --> 00:19:26,720
Yes.

296
00:19:27,220 --> 00:19:30,060
Here, you could live in happiness.

297
00:19:30,810 --> 00:19:33,860
Seeing you wish for such a world pains me.

298
00:19:35,070 --> 00:19:36,900
I'm sorry, Archi.

299
00:19:37,570 --> 00:19:39,700
Why do you wish for that future?

300
00:19:41,110 --> 00:19:42,820
I want to be an admirable person.

301
00:19:43,700 --> 00:19:44,700
Emilia...

302
00:19:45,240 --> 00:19:47,870
Like Mother Fortuna, my role model.

303
00:19:48,330 --> 00:19:51,040
Like Geuse, who's so kind and strong.

304
00:19:51,540 --> 00:19:57,380
Like Archi, who kept smiling until 
the very end so I wouldn't be scared.

305
00:19:59,130 --> 00:20:03,220
Like Puck, who always protected 
me and never left me alone.

306
00:20:03,640 --> 00:20:05,220
Like Ram, who wished to do

307
00:20:05,220 --> 00:20:09,730
the one thing that would be most helpful 
to the one most precious to her.

308
00:20:10,310 --> 00:20:13,900
Like Otto-kun, who does his 
very best for his friends.

309
00:20:14,520 --> 00:20:18,280
Like Garfiel, who never once 
uttered a word of complaint.

310
00:20:19,230 --> 00:20:20,990
Like Subaru, who says he loves me

311
00:20:20,990 --> 00:20:25,030
and does reckless things even when 
he's all wounded and hurting.

312
00:20:26,530 --> 00:20:29,240
I want to look admirable to all of them.

313
00:20:29,700 --> 00:20:33,460
From now on, I want to be the one 
reaching out to help someone.

314
00:20:34,420 --> 00:20:36,130
So I'll be fine.

315
00:20:36,710 --> 00:20:40,050
I'm not afraid of the outside 
world, or of the future.

316
00:20:41,300 --> 00:20:43,180
Thank you for worrying about me.

317
00:20:44,340 --> 00:20:48,140
I'm just fine, Archi-oniichan.

318
00:20:53,480 --> 00:20:55,980
You're such a stubborn girl.

319
00:20:55,980 --> 00:21:00,360
You have no idea how crazy that made 
things for Fortuna-sama and me.

320
00:21:00,990 --> 00:21:03,530
S-So sorry about that...

321
00:21:03,530 --> 00:21:05,160
It's all right. After all...

322
00:21:06,030 --> 00:21:09,200
A big brother should always 
spoil his little sister.

323
00:21:10,410 --> 00:21:12,620
Thanks, Onii-chan!

324
00:21:20,960 --> 00:21:25,430
Thank you for showing this 
world to me, Echidna.

325
00:21:27,590 --> 00:21:30,600
I never thought I'd get 
to see the two of them,

326
00:21:30,600 --> 00:21:36,400
Mother and Geuse... Father... 
laughing together like that.

327
00:21:37,270 --> 00:21:37,900
So...

328
00:21:38,770 --> 00:21:39,650
Thank you.

329
00:21:41,860 --> 00:21:42,820
You...

330
00:21:44,400 --> 00:21:45,280
Echidna?

331
00:21:47,990 --> 00:21:49,530
You disgust me.

332
00:21:50,950 --> 00:21:54,290
I just... hate you so much.

333
00:22:20,980 --> 00:22:23,230
Don't come near us, witch! Go away!

334
00:22:23,230 --> 00:22:24,490
Filthy woman!

335
00:22:39,210 --> 00:22:44,130
Just how much have I been protected 
by others all this time?

336
00:22:59,100 --> 00:23:00,060
<i>Well, look at that.</i>

337
00:23:04,230 --> 00:23:08,320
<i>I look less like Mother Fortuna that I thought.</i>

338
00:23:08,990 --> 00:23:10,160
<i>Too bad.</i>

339
00:23:20,250 --> 00:23:21,170
Huh?

340
00:23:21,380 --> 00:23:23,170
There she is!

341
00:23:21,960 --> 00:23:24,000
I'm so glad you're safe!

342
00:23:23,170 --> 00:23:24,500
You aren't hurt, are you?

343
00:23:24,500 --> 00:23:26,880
The margrave was on the verge of death...

344
00:23:30,380 --> 00:23:32,390
Thank you for worrying about me.

345
00:23:32,850 --> 00:23:34,720
I'm perfectly all right.

346
00:23:35,310 --> 00:23:37,020
I'm not hurt at all.

347
00:23:37,390 --> 00:23:39,560
But... I'm sorry.

348
00:23:39,940 --> 00:23:43,440
All the trials still aren't over yet.

349
00:23:44,110 --> 00:23:47,610
But Subaru and the others probably 
told you the news, right?

350
00:23:47,990 --> 00:23:52,110
There's no reason to keep all of 
you in this Sanctuary anymore.

351
00:23:52,110 --> 00:23:55,370
I'm going to get rid of the barrier,

352
00:23:55,370 --> 00:23:57,700
but you can go back to where your families...

353
00:23:56,870 --> 00:23:58,500
Subaru-sama and the others?

354
00:23:58,500 --> 00:24:00,960
Wait, did they tell us anything?

355
00:24:00,960 --> 00:24:03,380
Uh, I can't really remember...

356
00:24:03,380 --> 00:24:03,960
Huh?

357
00:24:05,790 --> 00:24:08,090
So you see, Emilia-sama,

358
00:24:08,090 --> 00:24:10,670
we will be waiting here, as promised.

359
00:24:16,890 --> 00:24:23,940
And we are not the only ones who 
have high hopes for your success.

360
00:24:26,610 --> 00:24:27,270
Huh?

361
00:24:28,610 --> 00:24:31,740
Ryuzu-san and the people 
from the Sanctuary...

362
00:24:31,740 --> 00:24:36,530
It appears safe to assume you've 
overcome the second trial.

363
00:24:37,870 --> 00:24:40,410
I must first offer my gratitude for that.

364
00:24:41,040 --> 00:24:44,960
And after hearing from Young Gar
 and the villagers,

365
00:24:44,960 --> 00:24:48,630
the voices of both the 
inside and the outside,

366
00:24:48,630 --> 00:24:52,470
we were finally able to get 
up and move on our own.

367
00:24:54,510 --> 00:24:57,890
To be honest, we're struggling 
to make up our minds

368
00:24:58,680 --> 00:25:01,230
about whether or not we can trust you.

369
00:25:02,980 --> 00:25:07,360
But we all heard Garfiel, 
that young boy, shouting in anger.

370
00:25:07,940 --> 00:25:11,900
When I realized how he must have felt,
 the hard worker that he is...

371
00:25:12,900 --> 00:25:14,780
It makes me feel so pathetic.

372
00:25:15,490 --> 00:25:19,620
He's still a child of fourteen,
 yet he was so...

373
00:25:20,790 --> 00:25:22,120
That boy deserves our praise.

374
00:25:23,120 --> 00:25:27,750
And Emilia-sama, the same goes for you.

375
00:25:27,750 --> 00:25:30,460
So... please let us bear witness.

376
00:25:36,340 --> 00:25:37,390
Very well.

377
00:25:37,890 --> 00:25:39,680
I'll come through this trial in one piece,

378
00:25:39,680 --> 00:25:42,220
and then we can talk things over.

379
00:25:43,430 --> 00:25:45,520
Yes. That's a promise.

380
00:25:45,520 --> 00:25:46,400
Whatever may—

381
00:25:47,440 --> 00:25:49,610
Too long, too serious.

382
00:25:49,610 --> 00:25:52,230
And your tone bounced 
between polite and crude.

383
00:25:52,230 --> 00:25:53,940
You should be ashamed.

384
00:25:53,940 --> 00:25:55,950
I-I'm sorry, Elder.

385
00:25:57,660 --> 00:26:01,160
Regardless, you have now heard our opinions.

386
00:26:01,160 --> 00:26:04,290
This is... hm? What is it?

387
00:26:05,620 --> 00:26:11,050
Um... When I heard him call you "Elder"...

388
00:26:11,750 --> 00:26:13,050
It just surprised me.

389
00:26:18,970 --> 00:26:21,470
I still don't quite feel 
satisfied with this, but...

390
00:26:22,350 --> 00:26:24,180
Right. Thank you.

391
00:26:25,020 --> 00:26:26,730
I feel like I can do my very best.

392
00:26:27,190 --> 00:26:30,400
If we've been of help, 
we could ask for nothing better.

393
00:26:31,190 --> 00:26:34,530
I understand the next trial will be the last.

394
00:26:34,530 --> 00:26:36,990
Yeah. I'm going to start very soon.

395
00:26:36,990 --> 00:26:41,030
But... Ryuzu-san, do you know where Ram is?

396
00:26:41,580 --> 00:26:44,950
Ram had to do a job that 
could not be put aside.

397
00:26:44,950 --> 00:26:45,950
A job?

398
00:26:47,670 --> 00:26:51,840
"Emilia-sama has her job, and I have mine.

399
00:26:51,840 --> 00:26:55,050
We will both see it through," she said.

400
00:27:04,520 --> 00:27:06,560
Well, I'm going in now.

401
00:27:09,940 --> 00:27:11,980
Take care!

402
00:27:11,980 --> 00:27:13,270
Good luck!

403
00:27:20,820 --> 00:27:23,410
<i>Face the disaster that is yet to come.</i>

404
